      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>A chat no longer shows Working while only a duckling is working, whether Claude is waiting on it or has finished its part. The ducklings bar shows the work and has its own Stop.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.27.11</h4><ul><li>When Claude hands work to ducklings and finishes its own part, the chat settles: no Working line or stop button, you can message normally, and only the ducklings bar stays until they're done.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.27.10</h4><ul><li>The working glyph moves calmly and smoothly, with soft fades instead of blinks, keeps moving while Squeak isn't the front app, and is a little larger in the sidebar.</li><li>New threads start in Skip approvals.</li><li>A stream on the dashboard shows its working threads and the newest few, with Show more for the rest.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
